  "body": " Reaching the Airline Reservation Office   An automated audit of an airline reservation office establishes that during peak travel windows, the telephone lines are completely busy 60% of the time.      Suppose you are calling the office during the peak travel window. Find the probability that it takes you exactly 4 total attempts to get through to an agent for the first time. Write your answer as a decimal rounded to three decimal places.  Probability =       Correct! Treat as geometric: or as Negative Binomial with :            Now suppose that both you and a friend must each complete a separate reservation call to this office. If you take turns calling, find the probability that it takes a total of 4 tries for both of you to get through and reach agents. Write your answer as a decimal rounded to three decimal places.  Probability =       Correct! Treat as Negative Binomial with :           Again, suppose that both you and a friend must each complete a separate reservation call to this office. Calculate the probability that you encounter a busy line exactly 3 times before both of you eventually get through to an agent. Write your answer as a decimal rounded to three decimal places.  Probability =       Correct! Treat as Negative Binomial with :           Find the expected number of total combined calling attempts required for you and your friend to both get through. Enter your answer as an integer.  Expected Total Calls =       Correct! Using the expected value formula for a Negative Binomial with :        "
