  "title": "Alternative Definitions for Waiting-Time Distributions.",
  "body": " Alternative Definitions for Waiting-Time Distributions   Both the geometric and negative binomial random variables can be defined ed by tracking either the total number of trials or the total number of failures . Let us define the alternative frameworks:  Counting Failures:    Geometric: Let be the number of failures before the first success occurs.    Negative Binomial: Let be the number of failures before the -th success occurs.     Counting Total Trials:    Geometric: Let be the total number of trials required to reach the first success.    Negative Binomial: Let be the total number of trials required to reach the -th success.           Write an algebraic equation relating the random variables and , and another equation relating and .                 Use your answer to part (a), properties for expected value, and what you know about (counting total trials) to show that the expected value of (counting failures) is .      Use your answer to part (a), properties for variance, and what you know about (counting total trials) to show that the variance for (counting failures) is .      Use your answer to part (a), properties for moment generating functions, and what you know about (counting total trials) to show that the moment generating function for (counting failures) is .     "
